# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dynasty GM Football — environment
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: copy this file to .env and fill in a real connection
# string. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# VERCEL: this file is NOT read in production. Set these in the Vercel project
# under Settings -> Environment Variables. The Neon integration injects
# DATABASE_URL for you; the rest are optional and have working defaults.
#
# Full setup order, the one-time database baseline step, and rollback:
# see docs/deployment.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Postgres connection string.
#
# The app has no other required configuration. If this is missing or empty the
# app still starts, and then every page that touches the database throws
# PrismaClientInitializationError ("You must provide a nonempty URL") on its
# first query — the failure is deferred to request time, not startup. With
# `prisma migrate deploy` in the build script, a missing URL now fails the
# BUILD instead, which is the loud, early failure you want.
#
# On Vercel + Neon, use the POOLED connection string (the host containing
# `-pooler`). Serverless functions open a connection per invocation and a
# direct, unpooled Neon endpoint runs out of connections under even light
# concurrent use.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — creation limits (see lib/owner.ts)
#
# One league writes ~5,300 rows over 236 database round trips. These two
# ceilings are what stand between a free-tier database and one tester holding
# down the Create button. Both must be positive integers; anything else is
# ignored and the default below is used.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How many saves one browser (one owner cookie) may hold. Default: 8.
# This is a fairness/UX limit, not a security control — clearing cookies
# resets it, because the owner key IS the cookie.
# MAX_LEAGUES_PER_OWNER="8"

# Hard ceiling on leagues in the whole database. Default: 500.
# This is the one that actually protects the database, because it is the only
# one a caller rotating cookies cannot walk around. Raise it deliberately:
# 500 leagues is roughly 2.6 million rows.
# MAX_LEAGUES_TOTAL="500"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT SET BY YOU
#
# NODE_ENV — set by Next/Vercel. The app reads it in three places; the one
# that matters is lib/owner.ts, where production hides "unowned" legacy saves
# (ownerKey NULL) from every browser. Never set NODE_ENV=development on a
# public deployment: it makes every unowned save visible to every visitor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
